     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi INLA,<div><br></div><div>I have a question about implementing the multinomial-poisson transform  with a spatial model.   If I implement the following multinomial approximation model:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">formula = y ~ -1 +</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">   ## one intercept pr multinom observation</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">   f(idx, model=&quot;iid&quot;,</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    hyper = list(</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">   </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">prec = list(</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">   </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">initial = log(0.000001),</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">   </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">fixed = TRUE))) +</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">f(jdx, x, model=&quot;iid&quot;,</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">## beta&#39;s sum to zero?</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">constr = sum.to.zero,</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">hyper = list(</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">prec = list(</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">initial = log(0.001),</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\">fixed = TRUE)))</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;font-size:13.63636302948px\"><br></span></div><div>Could one use the copy command to add a spatial random effect for each of the jdx groups in the Multinomial?  for example using something like that found in the DLM example  (<a href=\"http://www.math.ntnu.no/inla/r-inla.org/papers/DLM_examples_2011-10-23.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.math.ntnu.no/inla/r-inla.org/papers/DLM_examples_2011-10-23.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792446011831000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Vp_217Qm18FfcDO_UfFP-\">http://www.math.ntnu.no/inla/r-inla.org/papers/DLM_examples_2011-10-23.R</a>)?  Specifically, I&#39;m looking at this part, which provides the temporal link between observations:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"> + f(jdx, model=&quot;iid&quot;, initial=-10, fixed=T) +\r\n   f(j, w1, copy=&quot;i&quot;)</pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">Many thanks for the software and the help,</pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">Tom </pre></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
